@startuml ArchitectureDiagram
title CakeQueue architecture (simplified)

package "Entry" {
  [Duke] as Duke
}
package "UI" {
  [BakerCli] as Baker
}
package "Parsing" {
  [Parser] as Parser
}
package "Commands" {
  [XYZCommand] as Cmd
}
package "Model" {
  [OrderList] as List
  [Order] as Order
}
package "Storage (v2.0)" {
  [Storage] as Storage
}
database "data/cakequeue.txt" as File

Duke --> Baker : runs
Baker --> Parser : parse baker input
Baker --> Cmd : create + execute
Cmd --> List : read / update
List "1" --> "0..*" Order : stores
Duke --> Storage : load at start,\nsave after each change
Storage --> File : read / write
note right of Cmd
  Placeholder for the concrete
  command classes, e.g.
  FindCommand, MarkCommand.
  Each returns a String message;
  the CLI prints it.
end note
note bottom of Duke
  The shared OrderList is loaded
  once and passed to BakerCli.
end note
@enduml
